  "caption": "10pm: Quinn's watch said 4,212 steps, so Quinn marched laps of the lounge room and collapsed at 9,987.\n\nThe 10,000 figure began as a 1960s marketing number. Research suggests much of the benefit comes from moving from very low step counts up to around 6–8 thousand, so steps under 10,000 absolutely count.\n\nWhat can help: aim for any steady increase, try 7–8 thousand if you like a target, include some brisk minutes, add two strength sessions a week, and build walking gradually if you're coming back from an injury.\n\nGet it checked if knee or hip pain rises as your walking volume goes up.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
